# The visualizer is stamped INSIDE the target repo, so everything bun and vite
# generate here lands in that repo's working tree. permissions.snapshot() reads
# untracked files with `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`, so an
# unignored artifact tree is indistinguishable from an agent writing to the repo:
# `just obs` runs `bun install`, and a run watched that way had its planner phase
# killed by a 5671-path breach whose rollback unlinked every dependency file.
#
# This lives beside the app rather than in the root .gitignore so the scope is
# exactly the visualizer — a root-level `dist/` would also swallow build output
# belonging to the host repo. It travels with the app to every integration
# directory, so .claude, .agents, and .kiro are covered without naming any.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
